[2026-01-30T00:36:02.559Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01L7GeCiDRzCR1deX1SMQ6jp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully executed the requirement file **idea-gen-1769729285840-ctx_1769-po** (Performance for Report Tabs).\n\n**Summary:**\n- **Scan created:** `bc19a751-01aa-46da-8a68-2aba0abf449d`\n- **5 ideas saved to Vibeman**\n\n**Ideas Generated:**\n\n1. **Virtualize FindingsTab list for large datasets** - Reports with 100+ findings need react-window virtualization to keep DOM light and scrolling smooth\n\n2. **Memoize sourceMap creation in FindingsTab** - Filtering logic runs synchronously on main thread; consider Web Worker or pagination for large datasets\n\n3. **Debounce search input in FindingsTab and SourcesTab** - Filter recalculation on every keystroke causes lag; 150-200ms debounce reduces recalculations by 80-90%\n\n4. **Pre-compute entity grouping in EntitiesTab** - O(n) grouping runs on every render; move to data fetch time for instant tab switches\n\n5. **Use React.memo on FindingCard and SourceRow components** - List items re-render unnecessarily when filters change; memoization prevents wasted renders\n\n**Observations:**\n- Lists render without virtualization - problematic at scale\n- Search inputs trigger immediate state updates without debouncing\n- Entity grouping computation happens on render rather than data fetch\n- List item components (FindingCard, SourceRow) lack memoization\n- All filtering runs synchronously on main thread"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3356,"cache_read_input_tokens":163185,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3356},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05d3e4f1-2259-4f3e-a055-8040a34c8b02","uuid":"9f04bbe3-2e0a-4439-b774-7484a4fd63a7"}
